// Correlation on a NESTED reserved field (author-chosen hierarchy).
//
// The custom event schema (event.dwschema) injects `__drupe` as a
// nested group with a `sessionid` member. A Read is permitted only if there
// was formerly a Login in the SAME session — the past Login's
// `__drupe.sessionid` must equal the current Read's, referenced via the
// generic `context.__drupe.sessionid` path. This exercises a nested
// injected/reserved field end to end (it is not request scope, so it is
// reached by its own dotted path, unlike principal).
//
// Positive/negative control across two traces:
//   trace_1: the prior Login shares the Read's session → permitted.
//   trace_2: IDENTICAL except the prior Login is a different session → the
//            correlation fails → NOT permitted.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{
        input.user: context.input.user,
        __drupe.sessionid: context.__drupe.sessionid
    }
};
